  "articleBody": "A living room addition can create more usable space, improve daylight and make an existing home fit changing household needs, but the right plan depends on lot limits, structural connections, heating and cooling, natural light, and how the new room will relate to the rest of the house. Start with a defined use, measured existing conditions, and a provider who can coordinate design, permits, and construction.",
